# PLANT-COORD-01 MUTATION — THE ATOMIC TAKE REPLACED BY CHECK-THEN-WRITE.
#
# ================================================================================================= #
# **SUPERSEDED AT INCREMENT 13 BY `CD-ENG-COORD-FIX-01`, AND THE REASON IS RECORDED HERE BECAUSE A
# SEAT EDITING ANOTHER SEAT'S COUNTERFACTUAL MUST SAY WHY IN THE ARTEFACT ITSELF.**
#
# Increment 12 had ONE exclusion mechanism on a claim take: `O_EXCL`. Hunk 1 below removes it, and
# that was sufficient to admit two holders of one task — the contrast `PLANT-COORD-01` arm 2 needs.
#
# `CD-ASR-WO2R3-06-F04` forced a SECOND mechanism: the scope check and the take now run inside
# `registry.critical_section` (`fcntl.flock`). **SO HUNK 1 ALONE NO LONGER ADMITS ANYTHING** — with
# `O_EXCL` gone, the mutex still serialises the two racers and the second one still loses. RUN
# AGAINST THE FIXED TREE WITH HUNK 1 ONLY, ARM 2 REPORTED `*** DID NOT CONTRAST ***`, AND IT WAS
# RIGHT TO: a plant that passes both arms is DEAD and is worse than no plant.
#
# **HUNK 2 IS THEREFORE ADDED, AND IT MAKES THIS COUNTERFACTUAL STRICTLY STRONGER, NOT WEAKER.**
# The mutation must now defeat BOTH exclusion mechanisms to admit a double-take. Nothing was
# removed from hunk 1, no assertion was relaxed, and no arm's expectation was changed. **A MUTATION
# THAT MUST BREAK MORE IN ORDER TO FALSIFY IS A HARDER TEST OF THE CONTROL, AND THAT IS THE ONLY
# DIRECTION A SEAT MAY EVER MOVE A TEST IT DID NOT WRITE.**
# ================================================================================================= #
diff --git a/tools/coordination/registry.py b/tools/coordination/registry.py
index 7e768b3..352be4c 100644
--- a/tools/coordination/registry.py
+++ b/tools/coordination/registry.py
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ def critical_section(root: str, which: str, timeout: float = LOCK_TIMEOUT_S) ->
     try:
         while True:
